      ":question/problem": "![](images/a8/a8189300ed2ac0aa01c8c14cd762adccfb64cc29c93dc7d76f74a074b688d344.png)\n\nTriangles $ABC$ and $DEF$ each have two angles measuring $65^{\u2218}$, as shown above. Which of the following additional pieces of information is sufficient to prove that these triangles are congruent?\n\n1. The measures of $\u2220C$ and $\u2220F$ are equal.\n2. The lengths of $BC^(\u2015)$ and $EF^(\u2015)$ are equal.\n3. The lengths of $AC^(\u2015)$ and $DE^(\u2015)$ are equal.\n4. No additional information is needed.\n\n*(Note: Images not drawn to scale)*"
